WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:07.000
A voice may seem to change when the mouth moves differently.

00:00:07.000 --> 00:00:14.000
In 1976, researchers paired an audio syllable with conflicting lip movements.

00:00:14.000 --> 00:00:21.000
Some listeners reported a third syllable. Not everyone hears the same thing.

00:00:21.000 --> 00:00:28.000
The finding concerns audiovisual speech perception, not brainwave therapy.

00:00:28.000 --> 00:00:35.000
Ask what observers heard, what the recording contained, and what controls changed.

00:00:35.000 --> 00:00:42.000
Read the original study and try our free twelve-minute observation field note.
